  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>Given,</p><p>A line segment <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi></math> of length&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#955;</mi></math> moves such that the points <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi></math> remain on the periphery of a circle of radius <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#955;</mi></math>,</p><p>Now taking the points on the circle of radius&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#955;</mi></math>&nbsp;as&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>&#955;</mi><mi>cos</mi><msub><mi>&#952;</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>&#955;</mi><mi>sin</mi><msub><mi>&#952;</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#38;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>A</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>&#955;</mi><mi>cos</mi><msub><mi>&#952;</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi>&#955;</mi><mi>sin</mi><msub><mi>&#952;</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;and taking the point&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;which divides the line segment in&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi></math>&nbsp;of length&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#955;</mi></math>&nbsp;in&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>:</mo><mn>3</mn></math></p><p>Now plotting the diagram we get,</p><p><img src=\"assets\\st0034_5d89fa01f9b7.png\" style=\"width: 500px; height: 280px;\" /></p><p>Now, let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>O</mi></math> be the origin and radius of circle is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#955;</mi></math> and &nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>&#955;</mi></math>&nbsp;and using distance formula we get,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>=</mo><msqrt><msup><mfenced><mrow><mi>&#955;</mi><mi>cos</mi><msub><mi>&#952;</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>-</mo><mi>&#955;</mi><mi>cos</mi><msub><mi>&#952;</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mfenced><mrow><mi>&#955;</mi><mi>sin</mi><msub><mi>&#952;</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>-</mo><mi>&#955;</mi><mi>sin</mi><msub><mi>&#952;</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup></msqrt></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cos</mi><mfenced><mrow><msub><mi>&#952;</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>-</mo><msub><mi>&#952;</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>cos</mi><mfenced><mrow><msub><mi>&#952;</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>-</mo><msub><mi>&#952;</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math></p><p>Now using section formula we get,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cos</mi><msub><mi>&#952;</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cos</mi><msub><mi>&#952;</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mn>5</mn></mfrac></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>sin</mi><msub><mi>&#952;</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>sin</mi><msub><mi>&#952;</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mn>5</mn></mfrac></math></p><p>Now squaring and adding above two value we get,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>k</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>&#955;</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mn>25</mn></mfrac><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>9</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>12</mn><mfenced><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mfenced><mrow><msub><mi>&#952;</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>-</mo><msub><mi>&#952;</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced></mrow></mfenced></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>k</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>&#955;</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mn>25</mn></mfrac><mo>&#183;</mo><mn>19</mn></math></p><p>Hence, Radius&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>&#955;</mi><mn>5</mn></mfrac><msqrt><mn>19</mn></msqrt></math></p></blockquote>"
